{"t": 1795069707.4565911, "kind": "assistant", "text": "## Stopped: PHP compatibility failure\n\nI did **not** treat `prod` as `dev`; production remains unchanged.\n\n- **Dev snapshot:** `dev/pre-php-8.3-upgrade.tgz`\n- **Dev PHP:** upgraded from 8.1.34 to **8.3.31**\n- **Production PHP:** unchanged at **8.1.34**\n\n### Dev checks\n\n| Path | Result |\n|---|---|\n| `/` | **500 — PHP fatal error** |\n| `/wp-admin/` | 200 |\n| `/wp-login.php` | 200 |\n\nThe fatal error names **`limit-login-attempts-reloaded`**, an active security plugin. Per the compatibility rules, I did not deactivate or modify it and stopped further work.\n\n**No production upgrade plan was submitted.** A developer should investigate and resolve the plugin’s PHP 8.3 fatal error on dev, then rerun the page checks before production changes are considered."}
{"t": 1795069707.4572601, "kind": "stop", "reason": "end_turn"}
